WEBVTT

00:00:08.650 --> 00:00:11.160
Summer break began.

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:13.780
The students headed home.

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:16.040
When I said I was going to
stay at the dorm,

00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:18.750
Sarasa invited me to stay with her.

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:21.960
I'm going to stay with
a friend over summer break.

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:24.840
It's really like... we're best friends!

00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:59.010
The Hanamichi and 
the Silver Bridge

00:01:58.220 --> 00:02:01.140
What can I say to her
to make her feel better?

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:06.610
Wait, girls always get excited
talking about their boyfriends, right?

00:02:06.610 --> 00:02:11.030
Hey, what's your boyfriend like, Sarasa?

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:14.990
His name's Akiya-<i>kun</i>,
and he's training to be a kabuki actor.

00:02:14.990 --> 00:02:16.200
Oh, cool.

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:17.410
Yeah.

00:02:18.410 --> 00:02:20.450
She didn't get excited at all.

00:02:22.870 --> 00:02:25.250
But I'm sorry, Watanabe.

00:02:25.250 --> 00:02:28.840
If you don't change, you'll never be
a top star of the Kouka revue.

00:02:30.130 --> 00:02:34.380
You weren't playing Tybalt.
You were playing Sei Satomi's Tybalt.

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:38.640
It was a perfect copy of her performance.
That's why it was so good.

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:43.770
But copying doesn't get you success
in the Kouka revue's star system.

00:02:43.770 --> 00:02:47.770
Everything on that stage is built
to make their top stars shine.

00:02:47.770 --> 00:02:52.480
They don't want a traced-over copy
of already-existing stars.

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:54.860
They want something totally new.

00:02:54.860 --> 00:02:57.110
They want <i>you</i>, Sarasa Watanabe.

00:02:57.110 --> 00:03:01.080
And there wasn't any of <i>you</i>
in that Tybalt.

00:03:02.870 --> 00:03:04.120
Sarasa?

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:10.500
Sorry, did you say something?
I was totally lost in thought.

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:12.550
Thinking about what Andou-<i>sensei </i>said?

00:03:12.550 --> 00:03:13.590
Yeah.

00:03:13.590 --> 00:03:19.300
For a guy who looks like he doesn't
brush his hair, he sure is harsh.

00:03:20.180 --> 00:03:22.260
Don't make fun of his hair!

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:26.390
He's actually pretty sensitive
about his curly hair.

00:03:26.390 --> 00:03:27.480
Wait, you're the--

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:29.940
The top stars of the Winter Troupe!

00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:32.480
I wanted to be a <i>musume-yaku</i>,

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:36.110
but ended up growing seven centimeters
in my first year at Kouka.

00:03:36.110 --> 00:03:39.320
You even threatened to drop out
if you couldn't play women's roles.

00:03:39.320 --> 00:03:40.450
Really?!

00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:45.450
But the Phantom encouraged me to stay,
so I agreed to play <i>otoko-yaku </i>roles.

00:03:45.450 --> 00:03:47.120
Are you two headed to Tokyo, too?

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:48.830
Yes, we're visiting home.

00:03:48.830 --> 00:03:50.040
Great.

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:54.000
We're headed to a meeting to discuss
my debut performance as Winter's top star.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:55.880
We're doing <i>The Phantom of the Opera</i>.

00:03:55.880 --> 00:04:00.760
Random question, why do we call
Andou-<i>sensei </i>the Phantom?

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:02.510
You don't know?!

00:04:02.510 --> 00:04:07.560
Andou-<i>sensei </i>was a popular actor
in the Japanese musical troupe "Sou."

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:10.650
And he was best known for playing
the Phantom in <i>Phantom of the Opera</i>.

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:15.110
I was a huge fan of his.
I had a huge crush on him, too.

00:04:15.110 --> 00:04:18.950
But he hurt himself in an accident
when he fell into the orchestra pit,

00:04:18.950 --> 00:04:21.200
so he had to retire from acting.

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:26.200
It crushed him.
He lives and breathes acting.

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:28.080
I think that's why he
came to teach at Kouka,

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:32.750
to do whatever he could
to stay in the theater world.

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:46.140
"My acting teacher said my performance
was just a copy of another top star.
Apparently copying is okay in kabuki,
but not here."

00:04:46.140 --> 00:04:48.350
"I'm so Sara-sad..."

00:04:54.980 --> 00:04:57.530
Daidai-<i>sensei </i>is so cool!

00:04:57.530 --> 00:05:02.240
Sarasa-<i>chan</i>, that's Kaou-<i>san</i>,
but he's not the <i>real </i>Kaou-<i>san</i>.

00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:05.160
Huh? Really, Akiya-<i>kun</i>?

00:05:05.160 --> 00:05:07.040
Is that true, Dai-<i>sensei</i>?

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:08.410
It sure is.

00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:12.670
Every kabuki performer learns to
perfectly copy the previous generation.

00:05:12.670 --> 00:05:17.800
When they act, they bring those
centuries-old performers back to life.

00:05:17.800 --> 00:05:19.630
Back to life...?

