00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:38.150
Akiya Shirakawa

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:39.990
Akiya Shirakawa...
that's Sarasa's boyfriend.

00:05:39.990 --> 00:05:43.200
Ai-<i>chan</i>! Sorry that took so long!

00:05:45.950 --> 00:05:48.490
I'm home, Grandpa!

00:05:49.740 --> 00:05:53.710
You're early! I got you
your favorite <i>ningyo-yaki</i>.

00:05:53.710 --> 00:05:58.340
Grandpa, this is my roommate
I'm always going on about, Ai-<i>chan</i>!

00:05:58.340 --> 00:06:00.010
We're best friends!

00:06:00.010 --> 00:06:01.340
Best friends!

00:06:01.340 --> 00:06:06.140
Th-These are for you.
Thank you for letting me stay.

00:06:06.140 --> 00:06:11.520
How very kind of you. Come now,
no need to sit so formally.

00:06:11.520 --> 00:06:13.310
No, I insist.

00:06:13.310 --> 00:06:16.020
I'm her best friend. I have to
make a good impression!

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:19.020
Oh, hey, Sarasa,
you got someone upstairs--

00:06:19.020 --> 00:06:21.360
Hey! How've you been, Sarasa?

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:22.820
Welcome back, Sarasa!

00:06:22.820 --> 00:06:24.230
We missed you!

00:06:22.860 --> 00:06:26.030
Shou-<i>chan</i>, Keiko! It's great to see you!

00:06:26.030 --> 00:06:29.160
Sarasa-<i>chan</i>! You had
any of that Kobe beef yet?

00:06:29.160 --> 00:06:30.490
Kuma-<i>san</i>!

00:06:30.490 --> 00:06:32.450
Didja get even taller?!

00:06:32.450 --> 00:06:33.580
Did I?

00:06:33.580 --> 00:06:35.080
When's your big debut?

00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:39.000
C'mon, now, she's got
a while to go for that!

00:06:44.930 --> 00:06:47.340
Finally, some peace and quiet.

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:51.510
Sorry about that, Ai-<i>chan</i>.
I didn't mean to ignore you.

00:06:51.510 --> 00:06:52.890
It's okay.

00:06:52.890 --> 00:06:56.100
I can't feel my legs anymore.

00:06:56.100 --> 00:07:02.440
Ai-<i>chan</i>, I've gotta go tell
my grandma I'm back in Asakusa.

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:05.320
Do you mind if I step out for 20 minutes?

00:07:05.320 --> 00:07:06.280
Go ahead.

00:07:06.280 --> 00:07:08.320
I can't even move.

00:07:08.320 --> 00:07:13.910
My cat Nono-<i>chan </i>should be upstairs!
You can go play with her if you're bored.

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:14.830
Okay.

00:07:14.830 --> 00:07:16.410
If I can get up there.

00:07:28.260 --> 00:07:31.600
What? JPX?!

00:07:31.600 --> 00:07:33.060
Akiya Shirakawa.

00:07:33.060 --> 00:07:36.140
Huh? What?!

00:07:36.140 --> 00:07:38.520
Are you Sarasa's boyfriend?

00:07:38.520 --> 00:07:39.350
What?

00:07:39.350 --> 00:07:42.320
This is the first time
we're speaking, right?

00:07:42.320 --> 00:07:44.940
You can't just start off with that.

00:07:44.940 --> 00:07:48.320
I don't care how famous you are,
it's called having manners!

00:07:48.320 --> 00:07:53.580
I'm sorry. I'm not really
good with people.

00:07:54.830 --> 00:07:59.920
And Sarasa's the first friend
I've ever had. I was just curious.

00:07:59.920 --> 00:08:01.540
I'm really sorry.

00:08:02.420 --> 00:08:05.840
We've been friends since we were kids.

00:08:05.840 --> 00:08:08.430
We took traditional
dance lessons together.

00:08:08.430 --> 00:08:10.760
You'll have to hear the rest from Sarasa.

00:08:12.390 --> 00:08:14.510
I'm back, Grandma.

00:08:14.510 --> 00:08:17.520
Someone said those words to me again.

00:08:17.520 --> 00:08:21.440
If you don't change, you'll never be
a top star of the Kouka revue.

00:08:21.440 --> 00:08:23.690
It will never happen! Not ever!

00:08:23.690 --> 00:08:27.190
No way in the world will you <i>ever</i>
be able to play Sukeroku!

00:08:27.190 --> 00:08:32.530
The word "never" always
makes me feel horrible.

00:08:33.950 --> 00:08:37.250
"Never" is a curse.

00:08:46.800 --> 00:08:49.510
Hi, Tomoe-<i>sensei</i>!

00:08:49.510 --> 00:08:52.430
Sarasa-<i>chan </i>was two years younger than me.

00:08:52.430 --> 00:08:55.140
Her family ran a tatami shop,
and she was always bright and cheerful.

00:08:55.140 --> 00:08:56.770
Whenever she came for her lesson...

00:08:56.770 --> 00:08:59.600
Mind if I watch, Tomoe-<i>sensei</i>?

00:08:59.600 --> 00:09:02.350
Kouzaburou always came to
see her for some reason.

00:09:02.350 --> 00:09:04.400
Hey, Sarasa-<i>san</i>. Long time no see.

00:09:04.400 --> 00:09:08.190
I might. We're in the middle
of Akiya's lesson.

00:09:08.190 --> 00:09:11.950
Kouzaburou is married to
the only daughter of Kaou Shirakawa,

00:09:11.950 --> 00:09:17.660
15th of his name, national treasure
and head of the Satomi house and troupe.

00:09:17.660 --> 00:09:20.540
Tomoe-<i>sensei </i>is Kaou-<i>san</i>'s younger sister.

00:09:20.540 --> 00:09:22.670
My father is Kaou-<i>san</i>'s cousin.

00:09:22.670 --> 00:09:28.210
He used to be a kabuki actor,
but gave up and quit early in his career.

00:09:28.210 --> 00:09:31.340
I was born into this big kabuki family.

00:09:31.340 --> 00:09:35.050
So what're you learning, Akiya-<i>kun</i>?

00:09:35.050 --> 00:09:36.180
Yakko-<i>san</i>.

00:09:36.180 --> 00:09:39.270
Ooh, I wanna do Yakko-<i>san</i>, too!

00:09:39.270 --> 00:09:40.890
Can I do it, too, Tomoe-<i>sensei</i>?

00:09:40.890 --> 00:09:43.060
Sure.

00:09:45.360 --> 00:09:46.900
Kaou-<i>san</i>?!

00:09:47.900 --> 00:09:49.400
Daidai-<i>sensei</i>'s here, too!

00:09:49.400 --> 00:09:51.240
Can I watch you two dance?

00:09:51.240 --> 00:09:53.240
Huh?

00:09:53.240 --> 00:09:54.570
Okay.

00:09:57.870 --> 00:10:02.040
I started training to perform kabuki
this year, when I was eight.

00:10:03.620 --> 00:10:05.920
The kabuki world values bloodline,

00:10:05.920 --> 00:10:10.420
which meant that I was the most likely
person to become the 16th Kaou Shirakawa.

00:10:10.420 --> 00:10:11.550
However...

00:10:19.680 --> 00:10:21.470
Akiya! Are you okay?!

00:10:23.100 --> 00:10:24.640
Did you hit your head?

00:10:24.640 --> 00:10:27.360
S-Sorry, I'm okay.

00:10:27.360 --> 00:10:29.150
Are you okay, Akiya-<i>kun</i>?!

00:10:29.150 --> 00:10:31.400
Yeah. Sorry for messing up, Sarasa-<i>chan</i>--

00:10:40.240 --> 00:10:43.790
I always knew you had good balance,
but my goodness.

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:50.300
I heard Kaou-<i>san </i>came to
watch you dance today.

00:10:50.300 --> 00:10:52.840
Was that girl there, too?

00:10:52.840 --> 00:10:55.760
You mean Sarasa? Yeah, she was there.

00:10:55.760 --> 00:10:58.300
I like her a lot.

00:10:58.300 --> 00:10:59.640
Is that right?

00:10:59.640 --> 00:11:05.890
She's really good at dancing.
She's super strong, and has good balance--

00:11:05.890 --> 00:11:08.560
Sure, but she's a <i>girl</i>.

00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:10.650
My mom had noticed it, too,

00:11:10.650 --> 00:11:13.570
but I pretended not to.

00:11:13.570 --> 00:11:15.610
I had to.

00:11:15.610 --> 00:11:21.530
Akiya! A newbie like you's only here
'cause you're kinda related to Kaou-<i>san</i>!

00:11:21.530 --> 00:11:27.750
If Kouzaburou has a boy,
they'll throw you right into the trash!

00:11:32.090 --> 00:11:33.420
What?!

00:11:33.420 --> 00:11:36.840
I'm the only kid who can perform today?

00:11:36.840 --> 00:11:42.390
Yeah, all the other kids
came down with a bad flu.

00:11:42.390 --> 00:11:45.390
I have to go out there by myself?

00:11:46.980 --> 00:11:50.400
You'll be fine, Akiya.

00:11:50.400 --> 00:11:54.480
Thank you so much for inviting us today.

00:11:55.820 --> 00:11:56.990
Um...

00:11:56.990 --> 00:11:58.660
What's wrong, Akiya-<i>kun</i>?!

00:11:58.660 --> 00:12:01.370
But I have lines.

00:12:01.370 --> 00:12:04.290
If it's just me, then it won't be
like we practiced.

00:12:04.290 --> 00:12:06.040
What if I mess up?

00:12:07.040 --> 00:12:11.130
Akiya, you need to have more confidence.

00:12:12.500 --> 00:12:15.800
The acting world won't go easy on you
just because you're a kid.

00:12:15.800 --> 00:12:17.090
You'd better get it together.

00:12:17.090 --> 00:12:19.010
I know, but...

00:12:19.010 --> 00:12:22.510
It's okay, Akiya-<i>kun</i>!

00:12:23.600 --> 00:12:28.520
Whenever we played pretend kabuki,
you didn't mess up, not even once!

00:12:33.520 --> 00:12:35.070
Kaou-<i>san</i>,

00:12:35.070 --> 00:12:40.860
we need more than one <i>kamuro </i>for Agemaki,
or the procession will look off.

00:12:40.860 --> 00:12:44.910
Could we have Sarasa-<i>san </i>stand in?

00:12:44.910 --> 00:12:50.250
She and I have watched the <i>Sukeroku </i>DVD
together plenty of times at Tomoe's.

00:12:50.250 --> 00:12:54.460
She's memorized all the lines.

00:12:54.460 --> 00:12:55.800
Very well.

00:12:55.800 --> 00:12:56.630
Come here.

00:12:56.630 --> 00:12:57.880
Okay!

00:13:08.020 --> 00:13:10.980
Look, Akiya-<i>kun</i>, we match!

00:13:10.980 --> 00:13:13.690
Here, take this.

00:13:13.690 --> 00:13:16.520
Take a sniff. Doesn't that smell good?

00:13:16.520 --> 00:13:18.900
Do you feel a little better now?

00:13:18.900 --> 00:13:20.280
Oh, y-yes.

00:13:20.280 --> 00:13:22.530
It'll be your lucky charm.

00:13:22.530 --> 00:13:23.870
I can have it?

00:13:24.740 --> 00:13:30.910
Sarasa thinks it's so cool that a kid
your age gets to perform in kabuki shows.

00:13:30.910 --> 00:13:34.630
She's so very proud of you.

00:13:34.630 --> 00:13:37.460
We're going to walk out
onto the stage from there.

00:13:37.460 --> 00:13:41.760
Just do what Akiya does,
and look straight ahead.

00:13:42.760 --> 00:13:44.220
Close your mouth.

00:13:58.110 --> 00:14:02.030
No one had taught her
how to steel her gaze like that.

00:14:02.030 --> 00:14:05.950
She faced forward towards the audience,

00:14:05.950 --> 00:14:09.950
as if doing exactly that was
as natural as breathing.

00:14:09.950 --> 00:14:14.750
As if she was born with
something I didn't have.

00:14:14.750 --> 00:14:17.920
That girl was something else.

00:14:17.920 --> 00:14:22.470
You know they say she's
Kouzaburou's illegitimate daughter.

00:14:22.470 --> 00:14:24.090
How sad.

00:14:24.090 --> 00:14:30.890
If she'd been born a boy, she could've
been next in line for the Kaou name.

00:14:30.890 --> 00:14:33.770
She's Kouzaburou's daughter?

00:14:33.770 --> 00:14:37.610
And if she'd been born a boy, then I...

00:14:38.820 --> 00:14:39.980
Akiya?

00:14:39.980 --> 00:14:42.780
Oh. Hello, ma'am.

00:14:42.780 --> 00:14:47.530
I heard you made quite the effort
at the last performance.

00:14:47.530 --> 00:14:48.910
Kaou-<i>san </i>was very proud.

00:14:48.910 --> 00:14:50.120
He was?!

00:14:50.120 --> 00:14:54.210
Akiya-<i>kun</i>! I had my lesson
before you today!

00:14:54.210 --> 00:14:55.960
Oh, hey.

00:14:55.960 --> 00:15:01.130
I'm gonna go see a movie
with Grandpa Ken today!

00:15:01.130 --> 00:15:02.670
See you later!

00:15:03.550 --> 00:15:07.340
Sarasa-<i>chan </i>got to perform with me.

00:15:07.340 --> 00:15:11.100
Huh? So that second <i>kamuro</i>
was played by her?

00:15:11.100 --> 00:15:14.270
She did really good,
even though it was her first time.

00:15:14.270 --> 00:15:19.190
Someone even said that if she'd been
born a boy, she could be the next Kaou.

00:15:19.190 --> 00:15:21.570
That's how good she was.

00:15:21.570 --> 00:15:26.660
I knew I shouldn't have said it.
I knew what I was doing.

00:15:26.660 --> 00:15:30.740
But I was a child, and had no idea
that throwing a pebble in the pond

00:15:30.740 --> 00:15:33.200
would ripple out that far.

00:15:33.200 --> 00:15:35.210
Don't be stupid!

00:15:35.210 --> 00:15:40.420
It doesn't matter how good you are,
or how much natural talent you possess!

00:15:40.420 --> 00:15:43.050
It will never happen! Not ever!

00:15:43.050 --> 00:15:45.630
No way in the world will you <i>ever</i>
be able to play Sukeroku!

00:15:47.090 --> 00:15:49.140
Now, go. Leave!

00:15:49.140 --> 00:15:50.720
Go home!

00:15:52.810 --> 00:15:56.980
The next day, Sarasa-<i>chan </i>stopped
coming for dance classes.

00:15:56.980 --> 00:15:58.560
Then...

00:15:58.560 --> 00:16:00.110
Cut the bullcrap!

00:16:00.110 --> 00:16:05.820
We did <i>not </i>bring Sarasa here so she could
get traumatized by the lot of you!

00:16:05.820 --> 00:16:08.910
Sarasa will have <i>nothing </i>to do with you
from here on out!

00:16:08.910 --> 00:16:13.870
She's our little girl.
Find yourself another tatami shop!

00:16:13.870 --> 00:16:18.000
Kouzaburou kept his head
bowed the entire time.

00:16:22.790 --> 00:16:26.420
You're the kabuki boy
who's friends with Sarasa.

00:16:26.420 --> 00:16:30.550
Sorry about all that yelling.
Didn't mean to scare ya.

00:16:32.140 --> 00:16:35.060
Sarasa won't come here anymore.

00:16:35.060 --> 00:16:38.480
But I'm only cuttin' her off from kabuki.

00:16:38.480 --> 00:16:41.730
I hope you'll still
keep bein' friends with her.

00:16:41.730 --> 00:16:43.480
I-I...

00:16:45.980 --> 00:16:47.940
Near the end of summer,

00:16:47.940 --> 00:16:51.200
Sarasa-<i>chan</i>'s grandmother passed away.

00:16:51.530 --> 00:16:54.030
Funeral

00:16:54.530 --> 00:16:57.120
We weren't allowed to come to the funeral,

00:16:57.120 --> 00:17:01.170
but Kaou-<i>san </i>insisted we
pay our respects from a distance.

00:17:05.630 --> 00:17:07.340
Sarasa-<i>chan</i>...

00:17:10.720 --> 00:17:14.010
Kaou-<i>san</i>, it's...

00:17:14.010 --> 00:17:15.390
It's all my fault.

00:17:15.390 --> 00:17:16.850
Don't say that, Akiya.

00:17:16.850 --> 00:17:20.390
Hold onto that feeling.
It'll make you a better actor.

00:17:21.770 --> 00:17:25.610
I'm sorry. I'm so sorry.

00:17:29.110 --> 00:17:32.950
It's a little late, but here.
Happy birthday.

00:17:33.950 --> 00:17:38.290
The Last Burst Premier Skeleton
Taku-<i>sama </i>from <i>Floor Kings</i>!

00:17:38.290 --> 00:17:39.330
It's see-through.

00:17:39.330 --> 00:17:42.170
Thank you so much, Akiya-<i>kun</i>!

00:17:42.170 --> 00:17:44.000
Is it supposed to be like that?

00:17:44.000 --> 00:17:46.800
I've got one more present for you.

