00:17:50.540 --> 00:17:50.750
{=1}August Kabuki Series

00:17:50.840 --> 00:17:56.220
I'm playing Taura Tomimatsu.
Kouzaburou is playing Fukuyama Katsugi.

00:17:56.220 --> 00:17:59.430
And Kaou-<i>san </i>is, of course,
playing Sukeroku.

00:17:59.430 --> 00:18:02.730
Thanks, but I'm not allowed
to see kabuki shows.

00:18:02.730 --> 00:18:05.110
I asked Grandpa Ken
and he said it was okay.

00:18:05.110 --> 00:18:07.980
I have two tickets,
so take Narata-<i>san</i>, too.

00:18:09.190 --> 00:18:13.360
Sarasa-<i>chan</i>, you know that thing
you asked for advice for on Twitter?

00:18:13.360 --> 00:18:15.200
Oh, yeah.

00:18:15.200 --> 00:18:19.200
Kabuki typically involves the perfect
replication of famous performances,

00:18:19.200 --> 00:18:20.620
but it's not <i>all </i>replication.

00:18:20.620 --> 00:18:22.250
Huh?

00:18:22.250 --> 00:18:28.130
Sukeroku's a superhero story, built around
a cool guy getting his revenge.

00:18:28.130 --> 00:18:34.050
But you also get to see him
being helpless and compassionate.

00:18:34.050 --> 00:18:37.510
That was all new to the audiences
in the Edo period, and they ate it up.

00:18:38.470 --> 00:18:41.560
Even now, they're still trying
new things in kabuki.

00:18:41.560 --> 00:18:45.230
Half-finished plays by famous playwrights
are being adapted into new shows.

00:18:46.310 --> 00:18:50.940
I stopped doing kabuki
when I was six, so I had no idea...

00:18:50.940 --> 00:18:54.700
As we try these new things,
we need to maintain our old traditions,

00:18:54.700 --> 00:18:57.780
while also entertaining our audience,
as we have for centuries.

00:18:57.780 --> 00:19:02.450
Us actors need to have the dedication
to fulfilling those expectations.

00:19:02.450 --> 00:19:04.000
Dedication...

00:19:05.040 --> 00:19:08.590
I want to show you
my dedication, Sarasa-<i>chan</i>.

00:19:08.590 --> 00:19:10.800
Akiya-<i>kun</i>...

00:19:10.800 --> 00:19:13.380
Oh, I've gotta head out.

00:19:14.590 --> 00:19:19.300
Sarasa-<i>chan</i>, I'm not scared
to go out on stage anymore.

00:19:23.180 --> 00:19:26.810
Hey, how are you connected
to all this kabuki stuff?

00:19:26.810 --> 00:19:32.690
Oh, when I was six, I got to
perform in <i>Sukeroku</i>, just once.

00:19:32.690 --> 00:19:34.190
Even though you're a girl?

00:19:34.190 --> 00:19:37.660
Little girls are allowed
to perform in kabuki.

00:19:37.660 --> 00:19:40.700
I got to walk across
the <i>hanamichi </i>with Akiya-<i>kun</i>.

00:19:40.700 --> 00:19:42.240
What was it like?

00:19:42.240 --> 00:19:44.250
It was quiet.

00:19:44.250 --> 00:19:47.710
I felt the audience's gaze
like heat on my skin.

00:19:47.710 --> 00:19:49.460
We may have been in the same room,

00:19:49.460 --> 00:19:52.210
but up on stage, it was like
being in a different world.

00:19:53.090 --> 00:19:58.050
I felt as if I'd transformed
into someone else.

00:19:58.050 --> 00:20:01.600
But I don't know. I think I'm still...

00:20:01.600 --> 00:20:03.770
I want to go see the play.

00:20:03.770 --> 00:20:05.140
Huh?

00:20:05.140 --> 00:20:07.390
Take me to see the kabuki play.

00:20:34.920 --> 00:20:37.380
Look, it's Sukeroku's <i>deha</i>!
I'm so good at it!

00:20:37.380 --> 00:20:39.970
Yes, you sure are.

00:20:39.970 --> 00:20:45.270
When I grow up, I'm gonna be Sukeroku!

00:20:45.270 --> 00:20:48.810
Wow. I wish I could see that.

00:20:55.610 --> 00:21:00.450
I didn't know if her tears were
because of fond memories

00:21:00.450 --> 00:21:03.030
or something else entirely.

00:21:03.030 --> 00:21:08.830
I just hope she doesn't
regret coming tonight.

00:21:08.830 --> 00:21:11.540
Did you have a fun summer break?

00:21:11.540 --> 00:21:15.590
Yeah! Thanks for seeing us off.
I'll see you soon.

00:21:15.590 --> 00:21:18.300
Winter break isn't that soon, though.

00:21:18.300 --> 00:21:21.380
Are you going to
come with her then, Narata-<i>san</i>?

00:21:21.380 --> 00:21:22.590
Probably.

00:21:24.680 --> 00:21:27.770
I'm gonna go grab some lunch.

00:21:32.310 --> 00:21:34.650
Sarasa-<i>chan</i>, y'know,

00:21:34.650 --> 00:21:39.030
when you know what you want,
all you can do is move towards it.

00:21:39.030 --> 00:21:42.860
We've only just started
down our paths. It's okay.

00:21:44.870 --> 00:21:47.620
Even if we lose sight of
what we want sometimes.

00:21:47.620 --> 00:21:49.000
It happens to you, too?

00:21:49.000 --> 00:21:51.710
All the time, even when I was little.

00:21:51.710 --> 00:21:54.670
But I always decide to keep going.

00:21:54.670 --> 00:21:58.550
After all, there's only
one path to follow.

00:22:00.380 --> 00:22:03.510
I want to play Lady Oscar.

00:22:03.510 --> 00:22:04.390
Right.

00:22:04.390 --> 00:22:07.850
Please play Sukeroku, Akiya-<i>kun</i>.

00:22:07.850 --> 00:22:11.230
They're shaking hands? Aren't they dating?

